## JWT verification

`/api/v1` requires a bearer JWT. These routes stay public: `/health/live`, `/health/ready`, `/openapi.json`, and `/docs`.

This project only verifies externally issued HS256 tokens. It does not create users, passwords, login, refresh tokens, or RBAC.

Generate a local key and keep it out of git:

```bash
openssl rand -base64 32
```

Put the value in `AUTH_JWT_SECRET_B64` in a local `.env` that is gitignored. Also set `AUTH_JWT_ISSUER` and `AUTH_JWT_AUDIENCE`. Optional `AUTH_JWT_LEEWAY` defaults to 30s and is capped at 2m.

